---
import GuideArticle from '../../../../components/GuideArticle.astro';
import { routeOf, GUIDE_BASE, routeDetailHref, hasRouteDetail, canonicalRouteSummaryOf } from '../../../../data/phone.js';

const povo = routeOf('povo20-zero-base-2026');
const mobal = routeOf('mobal-japan-voice-2026');
const iiJ = routeOf('sakura-mobile-voice-2026');
const mobalCurrent = canonicalRouteSummaryOf('mobal-japan-voice-2026');

const guideRouteHref = (r: any) => routeDetailHref(r) || `${GUIDE_BASE}?route=${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}`;
const keepAliveHref = (r: any) => hasRouteDetail(r) ? `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/${r.id}/` : `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/#${r.id}`;
---
<GuideArticle slug="japan-sim-retention-guide"
  h1="Japan SIM retention and overseas limitations"
  title="Japan SIM retention: residency and overseas limits (2026)"
  desc="Compare Japan voice-number eligibility and keep-alive plans. Current Mobal Voice Lite is Japan-only, not an overseas receiving-SMS solution."
  lead="Keeping a Japanese voice number while outside Japan differs from buying a visitor SIM for use inside Japan. Identity eligibility, international roaming, paid subscription and named-app verification must be checked separately.">

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Start with the number and your legal eligibility</h2>
<p>Voice-capable Japanese SIM contracts have identity requirements, and not every visitor plan qualifies for continued overseas use. Do not assume that a product offering a Japanese 070/080/090 number can receive codes abroad. Check the exact product, accepted identity documents and where first activation is permitted before paying.</p></section>

{povo && <section class="gd-sec"><h2>povo 2.0 — if you have Japanese residency</h2>
<p>{povo.acquisitionSummary || 'KDDI digital brand, all-online.'}</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Keep-alive:</strong> {povo.keep?.action || ''}</li>
<li><strong>Window:</strong> {povo.keep?.intervalDays} days.</li>
</ul>
<p>Full evidence: <a href={guideRouteHref(povo)}>povo route record</a>. This remains a <strong>HOLD</strong> option for people who cannot satisfy Japanese identity and activation requirements. Some provider-documented overseas SMS capability does not establish eligibility for new buyers abroad.</p></section>}

{mobal && <section class="gd-sec"><h2>Mobal Voice Lite — for use in Japan, not overseas SMS</h2>
<p>The newer normalized Voice Lite plan is {mobalCurrent?.metrics?.keepCurrency} {mobalCurrent?.metrics?.keepYearCostOriginal} per year (¥990/month) with a ¥4,950 setup amount. It provides a real Japanese voice number but its current SIM/eSIM support terms say it is <strong>Japan-only, with no international roaming or Wi-Fi Calling</strong>. This is not a verified way to receive Japanese bank or app codes while physically abroad.</p>
<p>The old Mobal Voice-Only tariff in the directory is historical context; use the <a href={guideRouteHref(mobal)}>current research record and sources</a> rather than assuming older roaming or renewal behavior applies.</p></section>}

{iiJ && <section class="gd-sec"><h2>Sakura Mobile — legacy visitor research</h2>
<p>The older Sakura entry is not a complete, currently normalized overseas SMS-retention product. Identity acceptance, continued service, current renewal costs and codes from a named app remain unresolved in this record.</p>
<p><a href={guideRouteHref(iiJ)}>Inspect Sakura evidence</a> before considering it; do not treat a visitor product as a proven long-term overseas number.</p></section>}

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>If Japan does not fit</h2>
<p>If you only need a non-Japanese number, compare other real-mobile routes in the <a href={`${GUIDE_BASE}directory/`}>research directory</a>. Country-specific identity, activation, roaming and app acceptance still apply; a Hong Kong number is not interchangeable with a Japanese number for all services.</p></section>
</GuideArticle>
